WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.840
One of Hollywood's dystopian dramas has been
affected by a real-life pandemic.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.889
A Quiet Place Part 2, the long-awaited sequel
to director John Krasinski's hugely successful

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:15.129
horror debut, has been delayed due to growing
concerns over the COVID-19 outbreak sweeping

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:16.129
the globe.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.040
"What is going on?"

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.590
This news comes to us courtesy of the director
himself, who confirmed on social media that

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.680
the second film in the Quiet Place universe
- a dystopian world in which monsters attack

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.340
anyone who makes the slightest sound - will
be delayed from its international March 18th

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.340
opening.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.270
Beyond that worldwide release, the flick was
also slated for a March 19th release in the

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.010
United Kingdom and a March 20th opening in
North America.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.550
Plenty of films have seen their release dates
delayed, their production halted or suspended,

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:51.489
or their normal journey to theaters otherwise
disrupted by COVID-19, a mutation of the coronavirus

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:55.520
that has proven lethal to more vulnerable
portions of the population and which has a

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.769
higher rate of serious cases than the seasonal
flu.

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:03.649
However, in the wake of countries like Italy
pushing its citizens to enter a state of quarantine

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:08.080
which prohibits its citizens from attending
public gatherings or spending time in crowded

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.750
places, as well as outbreaks within the United
States, the entertainment industry is paying

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.750
attention.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:18.550
The plot of A Quiet Place Part 2 finds Evelyn,
played by Krasinski's real-life wife Emily

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.280
Blunt, trying to survive with her children
in the aftermath of her husband's death in

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.770
the first film.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.560
Delayed at seemingly the last minute, a new
release date for the movie was not immediately

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.560
announced.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.480
Paramount Pictures, the studio behind the
Quiet Place sequel, released a statement about

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.530
the film's delay:

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.600
"After much consideration, and in light of
the ongoing and developing situation concerning

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:43.180
coronavirus and restrictions on global travel
and public gatherings, Paramount Pictures

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:46.420
will be moving the worldwide release of A
Quiet Place Part II.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.820
We believe in and support the theatrical experience,
and we look forward to bringing this film

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.250
to audiences this year once we have a better
understanding of the impact of this pandemic

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.659
on the global theatrical marketplace."

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:01.810
Krasinski is back in the director's chair
for the second installment, and he also appears

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.530
in the narrative as his character Lee in flashbacks.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.690
In his statement about the film's delay on
Instagram, he kept things positive, writing,

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:12.780
"One of the things I'm most proud of is that
people have said our movie is one you have

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.150
to see all together.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.040
Well due to the ever-changing circumstances
of what's going on in the world around us,

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.390
now is clearly not the right time to do that.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.700
As insanely excited as we are for all of you
to see this movie...

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.980
I'm gonna wait to release the film till we
CAN all see it together!

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.850
So here's to our group movie date!

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:29.890
See you soon!"

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:34.120
It's safe to assume that the team behind A
Quiet Place Part II didn't want to take such

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.890
a drastic measure when it came to the film's
release, but with concerns over public safety

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.360
hitting a frightening high, it does seem like
they made the responsible choice.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.660
“There are people out there.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.040
People worth saving."

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.490
As the outbreak of COVID-19 continues across
the world, the United States is entering a

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:54.600
potential state of emergency, while other
countries are finding themselves on various

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.959
forms of lockdown to prevent any further,
potentially fatal spread.

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:03.080
Unsurprisingly, the film industry has been
hit hard, with tons of films facing filming

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.040
delays and halted releases.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.190
The newest James Bond film, No Time to Die,
was one of the first films to have its release

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.600
date affected by the crisis.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:16.860
As COVID-19 spread, Daniel Craig's final outing
as 007 was delayed by a whopping eight months,

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.630
getting a new November release date instead
of its original April premiere.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.390
As the United States faced its own emerging
COVID-19 cases when the virus spread outside

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.349
of Europe and Asia, new concerns grew, affecting
a number of other projects as well.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:34.440
Between filming delays on the next Mission:
Impossible movie, a temporary hold on production

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.880
on The CW's Riverdale, and the next Fast &amp; Furious
film getting delayed for an entire year, studios

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.660
are sparing no effort to keep people safe
as the pandemic sets in.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.500
Stay safe out there - we hope to see you at
the movies when this all blows over.

